course: dictionary
lesson: 5184
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Ivory can mean a material, a colour, or something quite different. The context tells you which meaning is right. «The elephant's ivory tusks gleamed in the sun» means the hard material, but «The bride wore an ivory dress» means a creamy off-white colour.
explain: Look for clue words around the tricky word. «He can really tickle the ivories on the piano» uses an informal phrase, and the word piano is your clue that it means playing the piano. «She lives in an ivory tower and never sees the real problems people face» means a place far away from real life.
explain: Always ask: what word would fit here? Then swap your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Ivory is a hard, creamy-white material that elephant tusks are made of.
fact: Walrus, narwhal and hippo teeth are also ivory.
fact: Ivory can also be a creamy off-white colour.
fact: «An ivory tower» is a place or life far from real-world problems.
fact: Selling new ivory is banned in most countries, including the UK, because poachers kill elephants for their tusks.
exercise: «Tusks are two very long front teeth made of ivory that grow all life long.» What is ivory in this sentence? | A kind of piano | A creamy off-white colour | *A hard, creamy-white material | A place far from real life
exercise: «The wedding dress was a soft ivory colour.» What does ivory mean here? | A tall tower made of stone | A hard material from tusks | *A creamy off-white colour | A type of piano
exercise: Sofia says, «She is living in an ivory tower.» What does it mean? | *A place or life far from real-world problems | A tall building made of white stone | A place where elephants live | Playing music very well
test: «He can really tickle the ivories on the piano.» What does tickle the ivories mean? | To tune a piano | *To play the piano | To clean the piano keys | To stop playing in a hurry
test: «Poachers kill elephants for their tusks, and selling ivory is banned in most countries.» What does ivory mean here? | *The hard material that tusks are made of | A tall tower far away | A creamy off-white colour | A piano key
exam: «The carved ivory chess piece was sold at an auction.» What does ivory mean here? | Playing the piano | A creamy off-white colour | A tall tower far from real life | *A hard material from animal teeth
